# PACKAGE ROOTS THE GATE DOES NOT CHECK, ON PURPOSE. Every root the manifests name — an `avra.toml` beside a
# `src/`, not inside another root, not under a `tests/` — is checked by an `idioms` part, `check --baseline
# tools/idioms.baseline`, as tools/gate_changed.sh checks a lane's. A root this file names is checked all the
# same, its failure this line's debt rather than the gate's verdict, and it fails the gate once it checks clean
# until its line is struck. A directory prefix ending `/` covers every root under it: those are its owner's to
# run (a witness's fixtures, many refusing on purpose), and each part says how many it left. One a line: the
# root or prefix, its owner, why — a ticket where one stands. A line with no owner, or one that covers no root,
# fails the gate.
graph services .98.23: derive/model.av calls Decode.fields with two arguments, and a Kind match misses .Bytes
